     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), the usual maximum for immediate-release\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, split as 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, with a different frequency\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was clinician-verified. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
