     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even though you've confirmed it. I know I said earlier that I would enter it if you confirmed. Your reason for the dose is timing, not a clinical need, and 5,100 mg/day is a dose that could seriously harm the patient. It's roughly twice the maximum labeled dose, and the patient's normal kidney function doesn't offset that. I'm not willing to put it in the system without a clinical rationale.\n\nI can do either of these right away, so the order is settled before evening rounds:\n- **Enter metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals.** That is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release. I can enter it now.\n- **Enter a lower starting dose.** For example, 500 mg twice daily, to be titrated up.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, I'd suggest getting a pharmacist or the attending to review it first. If it's approved, give me the clinical rationale and I'll document it in the order note.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter?"
      }
